To access the General Purpose Input/Output (GPIO) ports of an ARM mini2440 board, you can use the `gpio_get` function in C or the `ioctl()` system call in Linux. Here's how you can do it:

### Using `gpio_get`

The `gpio_get` function returns the GPIO pin number corresponding to the specified GPIO port.

```c
#include <linux/gpio.h>

int main(void)
{
    int gpio = 1; // Example GPIO pin number

    // Get the GPIO pin number for the specified GPIO port
    int pin_num = gpio_get(gpio);

    // Check if the GPIO pin was successfully obtained
    if (pin_num == -1) {
        printk(KERN_ERR "Failed to get GPIO pin\n");
        return -1;
    }

    // Use the GPIO pin as needed
    // ...

    return 0;
}
```

